<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the canopy-term-app binary: none, on purpose.

  It is a native window (winit, wgpu on Metal) around a terminal engine built
  ahead of time with Zig. It runs no JIT (allow-jit), records no audio
  (audio-input), loads no third-party libraries into itself
  (disable-library-validation) and needs no DYLD variables. tauri-bundler would
  sign an externalBin entry with the app's own entitlements (entitlements.plist),
  which is why this file is signed by scripts/prepare-sidecar.mjs instead, as the
  PTY host is (see pty-host-entitlements.plist).

  That the hardened runtime with no entitlements is enough for wgpu/Metal is
  expected, not yet proven on a real signed build.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
</dict>
</plist>
